Work:      Merlin Pro macro assembler, version 2.23
Author:    Glen Bredon
Publisher: Roger Wagner Publishing, 1984
Source:    https://archive.org/details/MerlinProMacroAssembler

The files here are vendor source code and its shipped object code, extracted
byte for byte from the distribution disk and used as test fixtures for the
Merlin assembler dialect. They are not compiled into, linked into, or
distributed with any Casso binary.

Casso itself is MIT licensed. These files are not, and the difference is
per-directory rather than per-repository. Two obligations follow:

  NO DERIVATIVES. Do not alter these files. Beyond the license term, an
  altered fixture is worthless as an oracle -- its entire value is being
  exactly what the vendor shipped. Tests MUST treat them as read-only. A
  mismatch is a finding about Casso, never a reason to edit a fixture.

  NON-COMMERCIAL. Anyone redistributing Casso commercially must remove this
  directory and the tests that consume it.

Provenance is verifiable rather than asserted: scripts/ExtractMerlinFixtures.ps1
re-derives every file here from a hash-pinned disk image, and README.md records
the expected SHA-256 of each.
